      "content": "thanks, it cut off at the end there but the distinction is coming through clearly. the realist section feels very structured and intellectually grounded—it uses actual IR theory which is perfect for a debate. \n\nthe idealist part, even though it's incomplete, already sounds way more like a series of grievances rather than a policy position. it's exactly what i was talking about—it feels like it's more about how people *feel* about the weapons rather than a strategic alternative.\n\ncan you finish that idealist section? and while you're at it, can you specifically highlight why the idealist arguments struggle to hold up in a professional policy debate compared to the realist one? i want to show my student how to point out that the latter is based on systemic reality while the former is often just an emotional reaction to a difficult situation.",
